## Fixes in the commit

- F611 and F631 (lesson-flow.tsx): min-h-11 on the "Open media" button and on the "Close"
  button of the media player. Every teacher control of the flow and the week view now reaches
  the 44 px floor.
- F632 (week-view.tsx): lang="en" on the family word picture caption, on the img alt holder
  and on the fallback span (an entry with no file). The bilingual helpers of the flow do not
  apply here: the caption is static English week data.
- F612 (docs/runbooks/storytime-deploy.md, flag section only): the flag-state bullet says that
  a revision cannot change, so the off command with the live image does not clear the flag
  from a new build revision that already carries it; a new build that shows the flag on
  (200 on /th/teacher/2/1 at its tag URL) does not get traffic as it is; the operator runs the
  off command with --image set to the image reference of the new build (read with the same
  imageDigest describe command on the new revision), checks the tag URL of the revision that
  this command makes (404 with the flag off), and names that revision in step 4. The old line
  "The variables must match, except the flag itself" now gives this action for the case where
  the new build holds the flag and the live revision does not. --no-traffic, the tags,
  Daniel's go, and the way back stay.
- F621 (same section): the env-compare command prints the variable names only
  (--format='value(spec.containers[0].env.name)'), and one line says the values are compared
  only for the flag and that the flag value is not a secret. No gcloud command ran; the
  runbook is text only.

